abstract: >-
  Code, notebooks, result tables and figures for an audit of five widely used
  public phishing URL benchmarks, showing that they encode collection
  conventions that inflate within-dataset results and can cause systematic
  cross-dataset prediction inversion, and that a simple pre-model audit
  exposes this.
keywords:
  - phishing detection
  - dataset bias
  - benchmark validity
  - cross-dataset transfer
  - machine learning evaluation
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sandesh20lamichhane/phishing-benchmark-audit"
